      "purpose": "Define retry ownership",
      "context": "Retries are scheduled by whichever worker last touched the delivery.",
      "thought": "One worker owns a delivery's retry budget at a time; ownership is a lease in the database, not a process-local timer.",
      "outcome": "Retry state moves out of the worker into the lease row.",
      "rationale": "A delivery must have one durable retry budget across all worker processes.",
      "next_action": "Choose where the claim boundary sits.",
